        "The evidence prevents temple-action scenes from being detached from festival travel and the material systems that supported sacrifice and pilgrimage.",
        "Josephus reports that Quirinius assessed Judean property after Archelaus's removal and that Judas opposed the assessment as enslavement.",
        "The account closely contextualizes Acts 5's memory of Judas while exposing rather than resolving the chronological difficulty posed by Luke 2."
      ],
